      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 752,
        "height": 352,
        "content": "## Manual Tagging (During the call)\nThis runs when someone manually adds the CSAT tag during the call.\nWe have added a waiting time of 120 mins in case this tag was added from an IVR option and the customer is still on hold."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d339ef70-41ad-4e5a-bd74-afdae9c5f74b",
      "name": "Sticky Note8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -816,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 624,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## CSAT Through NUACOM\n\n### How it works\n1. NUACOM trigger gets the calls and filters them out based on your selection.\n2. The call is Tagged to be included in your CSAT surveys. This can happen in many ways, automatically through this workflow, or manually by agents during or after the call, triggering the CSAT survey.\n3. Once the WhatsApp message is sent, it adds the call to a table to keep the Call ID allowing you to be able to reference it later through other flows, for example to reach back to specific calls.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Set up the NUACOM triggers by providing the NUACOM API Key.\n2. Enable WhatsApp in NUACOM and create a template for CSAT gathering.\n3. Select the CSAT template in NUACOM actions for WhatsApp.\n\n\n### Customization\nYou can customise the workflow and remove manual tagging for calls if you don't need it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
